.TH OPENMOVIEEDITOR 1 "2026-10-21" "de-xr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openmovieeditor \- native multitrack movie editor with QSV and side-by-side stereo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openmovieeditor
.RI [ project.vproj ]
.br
.B openmovieeditor \-\-render
.I PROJECT OUTPUT
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B openmovieeditor \-\-roundtrip
.I PROJECT COPY.vproj
.br
.B openmovieeditor \-\-export-srt
.I PROJECT OUTPUT.srt
.RB [ \-\-track " INDEX" ]
.br
.B openmovieeditor \-\-export-smil
.I PROJECT OUTPUT.smil
.RB [ \-\-track " INDEX" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open Movie Editor retains the original multitrack timeline, project library,
XML .vproj format, effects, node compositor, titles and render dialogs.
This de-xr fork uses DomeD's patched FLTK 1.4.5 and adds FFmpeg/libav QSV
media handling, per-clip stereo interpretation and mono/full/half SBS output.
.PP
Rendering and project/export commands initialize the original GUI engine and
require a display. Use
.B xvfb-run \-a
for batch work without a desktop.
The
.B \-\-help
and
.B \-\-version
commands exit before GUI initialization.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B \-\-render PROJECT OUTPUT
Render the edited timeline with its effects and audio.
Native FFmpeg output is finalized to a temporary file and published after success;
failure or cancellation preserves an existing destination.
.TP
.B \-\-roundtrip PROJECT COPY.vproj
Read and serialize an original-format project to the named copy.
.TP
.B \-\-export-srt PROJECT OUTPUT.srt
Export titles from the selected track as subtitles.
.TP
.B \-\-export-smil PROJECT OUTPUT.smil
Export the selected track in SMIL form.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print command usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the build version and exit.
.SH RENDER OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-encoder NAME
Video encoder. The added choices include av1_qsv (default), h264_qsv,
hevc_qsv, vp9_qsv and libx264. Availability depends on the FFmpeg build,
Intel device and driver. Encoding failures do not silently select software.
.TP
.B \-\-audio NAME
Audio encoder; default aac.
.TP
.B \-\-size WIDTHxHEIGHT
Per-eye display size; default 1280x720. Full SBS doubles stored width;
half SBS retains width and signals sample aspect ratio 2.
.TP
.B \-\-fps NUM[/DEN]
Positive rational or integer frame rate, no greater than 240 fps; default 24.
.TP
.B \-\-sbs mono|full|half
Override the project output layout. If omitted, use the project's stereo output.
.TP
.B \-\-quality INTEGER
QSV quality setting; default 23. VP9 uses bitrate/low-power settings instead.
.TP
.B \-\-bitrate INTEGER
Video bitrate in bits per second; default 8000000.
.TP
.B \-\-device PATH
Set the QSV render node for this invocation, overriding OME_QSV_DEVICE.
.TP
.B \-\-track INDEX
Select the zero-based track for subtitle or SMIL export; default 0.
.SH STEREO AND XR
The Stereo menu selects source layout and eye order and project output defaults.
Mono metadata takes precedence over filename hints; width alone does not select SBS.
The preview offers pair, individual-eye, anaglyph and packed-source views.
.PP
Convert 2D to SBS (Arc) invokes the installed arc-sbs converter asynchronously
before importing the result. It uses the existing model installation.
View edited timeline in mpvr / XR renders the timeline and launches mpvr with an
explicit stereo layout; mpvr and DomeD retain ownership of XR routing.
.PP
MKV retains stereo metadata most reliably. For MP4, use explicit player layout
selection or an _FSBS/_HSBS filename. The working compositor is 8-bit RGBA;
HDR management/export and a zero-copy effects pipeline are not implemented.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OME_QSV_DEVICE
Intel render node. This workspace defaults to
/dev/dri/by-path/pci-0000:03:00.0-render; choose the actual node on another host.
.TP
.B OME_HW_DECODE
Set to required to require hardware decoding, or off for software decoding.
The default attempts QSV and permits software fallback during decoder setup.
.TP
.B OME_AUDIO_BACKEND
Set to portaudio to skip JACK. Otherwise JACK is tried without starting a server,
then PortAudio is used.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Dome appearance is read from dome/appearance.json below this directory,
defaulting to ~/.config.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Root for openmovieeditor/previews, defaulting to ~/.cache.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Video Projects
Original project library used by the graphical Open, Save and Save As workflow.
Opening a supplied project imports it into the library without modifying the source.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/openmovieeditor/previews
Retained rendered XR preview files, unless XDG_CACHE_HOME overrides the root.
.TP
.I /usr/local/libexec/openmovieeditor
Default system installation's private executable and compatibility libraries.
The installation prefix and libexec directory are CMake options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Command-line engine operations return 0 on success and 1 on an exception.
Render/round-trip results and command errors include JSON on stdout/stderr.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
openmovieeditor project.vproj
xvfb-run \-a openmovieeditor \-\-render film.vproj film.mkv \\
  \-\-encoder av1_qsv \-\-fps 30000/1001 \-\-sbs full
xvfb-run \-a openmovieeditor \-\-export-srt film.vproj titles.srt \-\-track 0
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR arc-sbs (1),
.BR mpvr (1),
.BR xvfb-run (1)
.PP
README.XR.md contains release build, staging and installation instructions.
This source manual is not yet installed by the current CMake rules;
read it with man \-l doc/man/openmovieeditor.1.
